quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  58,1,"Indeed, Allah has heard the speech of the woman who disputes with you about her husband and complains to Allah. Allah hears the conversation of you both. Indeed, Allah is All-Hearing, All-Seeing."
  58,2,"Those among you who repudiate their wives (by zihar, saying to them: ‘You are to me like my mother’s back,’ they should know that) their wives are in no way their mothers. Their mothers are only the ones who gave birth to them. Indeed, they utter dishonourable words and falsehood. Surely, Allah is All-Pardoning, Most-Forgiving."
  58,3,"Those who divorce their wives by likening their backs to their mothers’ backs (i.e. zihar), then wish to retract what they have said, must free a captive before they touch each other. That is what you are advised to do. And Allah is All-Aware of what you do."
  58,4,And whosoever does not find the means shall fast for two consecutive months before they touch each other. And whosoever is unable (to do so) shall feed sixty needy persons. It is so that you may believe in Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him). These are the bounds set by Allah. And there is a painful punishment for the disbelievers.
  58,5,"Those who oppose Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) shall be disgraced as those before them were disgraced. And indeed, We have sent down clear revelations, and there is a humiliating punishment for the disbelievers."
  58,6,"The Day when Allah resurrects them all together, He will inform them about what they have done. Allah has kept account of it while they have forgotten it. And Allah is a Witness over all things."
